I go to the office kitchen.
I pour myself the coffee.
Sven is also in the kitchen.
He is the tester on our project.
We already know each other by face.
But we have not spoken much with each other yet.
"Hello Maya, welcome to the project!" says Sven.
"Thank you!"
"I am looking forward to working together," I answer.
He takes his cup and asks: "How do you like Berlin so far?"
"The city is great," I say.
"How long have you lived here?"
"I have lived in Berlin for a year," he explains.
"I moved here for this job."
We speak briefly about our work.
"I write the code and you find the bugs," I joke.
Sven laughs.
"Exactly!"
"Have you programmed anything today yet?" he asks.
"Yes, I have just started on it," I answer.
"When my code is ready, I will send it to you."
"Perfect, then I will test everything," Sven promises.
We drink our coffee and go back to work.
